Z||000000||Cheever2||07-19-2001||12:31 AM||||My car died (only a few blocks from home, thank goodness) and I discovered that my side-post battery cable connection screw is stripped and will no longer hold on tight enough to keep the car running.  In the short time I had to look at it before going to work, I could not tell how it comes off the end of the cable.<P>Do I have to replace the entire cable?  It's the positive side.<BR><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||4
Z||000001||My7Fieros||07-19-2001||02:07 AM||||The "round thing" (metal) that houses the screw parts pops out...you can buy replacements at Autozone. Easy fix.||||reg||1
